  "concept": "The village clothes shop of 1989 Everon: a draper on the ground floor of a two-storey town shop house, the shopkeeper living in the flat above. The base-game ShopHouse_E_2I01t with the vanilla clothes-store variant's doors, windows and ClothesStore fascia, and our own copy of its furniture with the shop-room clutter taken out. Three dressed mannequins stand in the shop window under spot lamps, the street signal at night (denim, a beige turtleneck with a red knitted hat, a green raincoat); a fourth, in a suit, stands inside. Folded shirts, turtlenecks, trousers and a denim jacket lie folded on the wall shelves, suit jackets and suit trousers folded on two display counters (piles of 3 to 5 folded copies, #1899), and hats, gloves and boots sit on their own shelf by the door. Everything is paid at the till, where a clerk in a suit stands. Base-game civilian clothes only: no military uniforms (KLMK and KZS belong to the gun store) and no _Dirty variants.",
